"file hierarchy as does the default \"poky\" distribution. If so, you "
"could update the :term:`SDK_TITLE` variable in the ``~/meta-"
"mydistro/conf/distro/mydistro.conf`` file using the following form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:172
msgid "Providing Updates to the Extensible SDK After Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:174
msgid ""
"When you make changes to your configuration or to the metadata and if you"
" want those changes to be reflected in installed SDKs, you need to "
"perform additional steps. These steps make it possible for anyone using "
"the installed SDKs to update the installed SDKs by using the ``devtool "
"sdk-update`` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:180
msgid ""
"Create a directory that can be shared over HTTP or HTTPS. You can do this"
" by setting up a web server such as an :wikipedia:`Apache HTTP Server "
"<Apache_HTTP_Server>` or :wikipedia:`Nginx <Nginx>` server in the cloud "
"to host the directory. This directory must contain the published SDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:185
msgid ""
"Set the :term:`SDK_UPDATE_URL` variable to point to the corresponding "
"HTTP or HTTPS URL. Setting this variable causes any SDK built to default "
"to that URL and thus, the user does not have to pass the URL to the "
"``devtool sdk-update`` command as described in the \":ref:`sdk-"
"manual/extensible:applying updates to an installed extensible sdk`\" "
"section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:194
msgid ""
"Build the extensible SDK normally (i.e., use the ``bitbake -c "
"populate_sdk_ext`` imagename command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:197
msgid "Publish the SDK using the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:203
msgid ""
"You must repeat this step each time you rebuild the SDK with changes that"
" you want to make available through the update mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:207
msgid ""
"Completing the above steps allows users of the existing installed SDKs to"
" simply run ``devtool sdk-update`` to retrieve and apply the latest "
"updates. See the \":ref:`sdk-manual/extensible:applying updates to an "
"installed extensible sdk`\" section for further information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:214
msgid "Changing the Default SDK Installation Directory"
