"configuration file. Doing so creates an SDK installer default directory "
"that applies across your distribution. As an example, assume you have "
"your own layer for your distribution named \"meta-mydistro\" and you are "
"using the same type of file hierarchy as does the default \"poky\" "
"distribution. If so, you could update the :term:`SDKEXTPATH` variable in "
"the ``~/meta-mydistro/conf/distro/mydistro.conf`` file using the "
"following form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:247
msgid ""
"After building your installer, running it prompts the user for acceptance"
" of the some_path_for_your_installed_sdk directory as the default "
"location to install the Extensible SDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:252
msgid "Providing Additional Installable Extensible SDK Content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:254
msgid ""
"If you want the users of an extensible SDK you build to be able to add "
"items to the SDK without requiring the users to build the items from "
"source, you need to do a number of things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:258
msgid ""
"Ensure the additional items you want the user to be able to install are "
"already built:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:261
msgid ""
"Build the items explicitly. You could use one or more \"meta\" recipes "
"that depend on lists of other recipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:264
msgid ""
"Build the \"world\" target and set ``EXCLUDE_FROM_WORLD:pn-``\\ "
"recipename for the recipes you do not want built. See the "
":term:`EXCLUDE_FROM_WORLD` variable for additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:270
msgid ""
"Expose the ``sstate-cache`` directory produced by the build. Typically, "
"you expose this directory by making it available through an "
":wikipedia:`Apache HTTP Server <Apache_HTTP_Server>` or :wikipedia:`Nginx"
" <Nginx>` server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:275
msgid ""
"Set the appropriate configuration so that the produced SDK knows how to "
"find the configuration. The variable you need to set is "
":term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:283
msgid "You can set the :term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS` variable in two different places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:285
msgid ""
"If the mirror value you are setting is appropriate to be set for both the"
" OpenEmbedded build system that is actually building the SDK and the SDK "
"itself (i.e. the mirror is accessible in both places or it will fail "
"quickly on the OpenEmbedded build system side, and its contents will not "
"interfere with the build), then you can set the variable in your :ref"
":`structure-build-conf-local.conf` or custom distro configuration file. "
"You can then pass the variable to the SDK by adding the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:298
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if you just want to set the :term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS` "
"variable's value for the SDK alone, create a ``conf/sdk-extra.conf`` file"
" either in your :term:`Build Directory` or within any layer and put your "
":term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS` setting within that file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:305
msgid ""
"This second option is the safest option should you have any doubts as to "
"which method to use when setting :term:`SSTATE_MIRRORS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:310
msgid "Minimizing the Size of the Extensible SDK Installer Download"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:312
msgid ""
"By default, the extensible SDK bundles the shared state artifacts for "
"everything needed to reconstruct the image for which the SDK was built. "
"This bundling can lead to an SDK installer file that is a Gigabyte or "
"more in size. If the size of this file causes a problem, you can build an"
" SDK that has just enough in it to install and provide access to the "
"``devtool command`` by setting the following in your configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:323
msgid ""
"Setting :term:`SDK_EXT_TYPE` to \"minimal\" produces an SDK installer "
"that is around 35 Mbytes in size, which downloads and installs quickly. "
"You need to realize, though, that the minimal installer does not install "
"any libraries or tools out of the box. These libraries and tools must be "
"installed either \"on the fly\" or through actions you perform using "
"``devtool`` or explicitly with the ``devtool sdk-install`` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:332
msgid ""
"In most cases, when building a minimal SDK you need to also enable "
"bringing in the information on a wider range of packages produced by the "
"system. Requiring this wider range of information is particularly true so"
" that ``devtool add`` is able to effectively map dependencies it "
"discovers in a source tree to the appropriate recipes. Additionally, the "
"information enables the ``devtool search`` command to return useful "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:340
msgid ""
"To facilitate this wider range of information, you would need to set the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:347
msgid "See the :term:`SDK_INCLUDE_PKGDATA` variable for additional information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:349
msgid ""
"Setting the :term:`SDK_INCLUDE_PKGDATA` variable as shown causes the "
"\"world\" target to be built so that information for all of the recipes "
"included within it are available. Having these recipes available "
"increases build time significantly and increases the size of the SDK "
"installer by 30-80 Mbytes depending on how many recipes are included in "
"your configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:355
msgid ""
"You can use ``EXCLUDE_FROM_WORLD:pn-``\\ recipename for recipes you want "
"to exclude. However, it is assumed that you would need to be building the"
" \"world\" target if you want to provide additional items to the SDK. "
"Consequently, building for \"world\" should not represent undue overhead "
"in most cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:363
msgid ""
"If you set SDK_EXT_TYPE to \"minimal\", then providing a shared state "
"mirror is mandatory so that items can be installed as needed. See the "
":ref:`sdk-manual/appendix-customizing:providing additional installable "
"extensible sdk content` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing.rst:370
msgid ""
"You can explicitly control whether or not to include the toolchain when "
"you build an SDK by setting the :term:`SDK_INCLUDE_TOOLCHAIN` variable to"
" \"1\". In particular, it is useful to include the toolchain when you "
"have set :term:`SDK_EXT_TYPE` to \"minimal\", which by default, excludes "
"the toolchain. Also, it is helpful if you are building a small SDK for "
"use with an IDE or some other tool where you do not want to take extra "
"steps to install a toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:5
msgid "Customizing the Standard SDK"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:7
msgid "This appendix presents customizations you can apply to the standard SDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:10
msgid "Adding Individual Packages to the Standard SDK"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:12
msgid ""
"When you build a standard SDK using the ``bitbake -c populate_sdk``, a "
"default set of packages is included in the resulting SDK. The "
":term:`TOOLCHAIN_HOST_TASK` and :term:`TOOLCHAIN_TARGET_TASK` variables "
"control the set of packages adding to the SDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:19
msgid ""
"If you want to add individual packages to the toolchain that runs on the "
"host, simply add those packages to the :term:`TOOLCHAIN_HOST_TASK` "
"variable. Similarly, if you want to add packages to the default set that "
"is part of the toolchain that runs on the target, add the packages to the"
" :term:`TOOLCHAIN_TARGET_TASK` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:26
msgid "Adding API Documentation to the Standard SDK"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:28
msgid ""
"You can include API documentation as well as any other documentation "
"provided by recipes with the standard SDK by adding \"api-documentation\""
" to the :term:`DISTRO_FEATURES` variable::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sdk-manual/appendix-customizing-standard.rst:34
msgid ""
"Setting this variable as shown here causes the OpenEmbedded build system "
"to build the documentation and then include it in the standard SDK."
msgstr ""

